A||||4||Cheever2||Saw many Fieros on my vacation||||7||
Z||000000||Cheever2||07-15-2001||11:42 AM||||Drove 545 miles from Houston to Gulf Shores Alabama, and didn't see a single Fiero on the highway going there or returning.  But there and at Pensacola Florida, I saw a total of 8:<BR>Red coupe in Foley, AL<BR>Yellow SE in Foley<BR>Red coupe in Gulf Shores<BR>Purple GT in Pensacola (plates said "PEGASIX")<BR>Black coupe in Pensacola<BR>Gold coupe in Pensacola<BR>Red GT in Elberta, AL<BR>Black coupe at used car lot in Foley<P>I'll have some pics of the yellow one and the purple one here someday.  After seeing the yellow car in a parking lot, I went to my minivan to write a note for their windshield, but meanwhile the owner came back and drove away!  That'll teach me to always have a PFF card ready!<P>I was very encouraged to see so many being well cared for.  Only one of those was rough.  Before leaving, I checked FOLD and found a lot of owners in Pensacola, but don't know if they have a club.<P>A little off-topic note: while in Pensacola, going to see the Blue Angels practice (at the beach where a shark bit off a kid's arm a few days before), we saw a mint 70(?) Cuda 340 get in a race with a 90's 5.0 Mustang right in front of us.  Cuda won of course.<P>------------------<BR>- <I>Chuck Hodges</I> -<BR><A HREF="http://home.houston.rr.com/fieropartsrelay" TARGET=_blank> Fiero Parts Relay</A> administrator||||reg||7
Z||000001||Raydar||07-15-2001||12:09 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>...we saw a mint 70(?) Cuda 340 get in a race with a 90's 5.0 Mustang right in front of us.  Cuda won of course.<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Heheheheheheh  ::THWAP:: <P>Bet it was nice down there, this time of year.<BR>We were in Gulfport last summer. Played on the beach and in the casinos. Only saw one Fiero, that I remember. <BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000002||StuGood||07-15-2001||02:03 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Cheever2:<BR><B>..we saw a mint 70(?) Cuda 340 get in a race with a 90's 5.0 Mustang right in front of us.  Cuda won of course.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><BR>Well, yeah...  Cuda shoulda.<P>||||reg||12
Z||000003||Wolfhound||07-15-2001||07:00 PM||||Cheever, Did you make it to the Original Oyster House while you were there? Good sea food and a hell of a collection of antique outboards, mounted on the walls.<BR>Coy ||||reg||14
Z||000004||Cheever2||07-15-2001||07:24 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>the Original Oyster House<HR></BLOCKQUOTE>No, but the guy we rented the beach condo from recommended it also.  We just never made it there.  We were on a tight budget and didn't eat out.  Me & Cheeverette want to go back next year without the kids (Cheeverlings?) and eat out, shop and see the sights we didn't have time for this week.  Besides the beach and the condo's private pool, we went to the less expensive places this time, like Fort Morgan, the ferry across Mobile Bay, and the Naval Air Museum which was excellent.  It was our first real vacation trip in many years.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Cheever2 (edited 07-15-2001).]||||reg||6
